      "description": "Watch Lecce vs AS Roma highlights and goals from Serie A on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 31, 2026. The atmosphere at the Stadio Via del Mare was electric as fans gathered for this highly anticipated Serie A clash. With both sides looking to establish their rhythm early in the season, the tactical battle promised to be a fascinating watch on the pitch. Early Dominance from the Visitors On August 31, 2026 , AS Roma displayed a ruthless edge from the opening whistle. It took only four minutes for the deadlock to be broken when a defensive lapse by Kialonda Gaspar gifted an opportunity to Donyell Malen , who clinicaly finished with his right foot. Although Malen picked up a yellow card for a handball shortly after, his impact remained significant. In the 23rd minute, Wesley provided a perfectly weighted assist for Malen to grab his second of the game. The momentum stayed firmly with the capital club as Matias Soule added a third goal just two minutes later with a sharp left-footed strike, leaving the home crowd stunned. Managing the Lead and VAR Drama As the match progressed into the second half, Roma focused on controlling the tempo through tactical substitutions. The introduction of Rodrigo Mora added fresh energy to the attack, and he was rewarded in the 65th minute. After receiving a pass from Gianluca Mancini , Mora found the back of the net. The goal was briefly put on hold for a VAR check, but after a review, the referee confirmed the goal stood, effectively ending any hopes of a Lecce comeback. The home side attempted to respond by bringing on Youssef Maleh and Ivan Ilic , but they struggled to break down a well-organized defensive line. Professional Finish under the Lights The closing stages of the match saw Roma maintain their grip on the game, recording a final possession stat of 65%. Frustrations boiled over for Lecce in the 90th minute when Ivan Ilic received a yellow card for a tactical foul on Mora . Despite late attempts by the hosts to create chances, goalkeeper Mile Svilar remained alert, claiming crosses and organizing his box with confidence. In front of 27,031 spectators, the referee brought the contest to a close after five minutes of added time, sealing a deserved and comprehensive victory for AS Roma ."
